  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased use of monitoring and evaluation information for RBM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This regional outcome contributes to strengthened institutional performance and governance through the systematic use of monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E) data in decision-making processes. While M&amp;E systems are in place, their integration into leadership and management decisions remains uneven, limiting their effectiveness for learning, accountability and programme improvement.

It aims to deliver the following results: (i) strengthened institutional M&amp;E systems, ensuring that evaluation findings systematically inform strategic decision-making and oversight; (ii) enhanced use of evaluation evidence by ILO leadership and project managers for policy development, risk management and adaptive programme management; and (iii) improved transparency and accountability through more timely evaluations and increased implementation of recommendations.

To achieve these results, the initiative supports improved quality, timeliness and use of evaluations, and promotes alignment of M&amp;E with organizational learning needs. It also encourages the adoption of data-driven approaches, including the use of sex-disaggregated data and gender-responsive evaluation methods.

This Regional Outcome contributes to key ILO cross-cutting policy drivers by strengthening alignment with international labour standards, promoting gender equality and non-discrimination, supporting informed social dialogue through knowledge sharing with tripartite constituents, and integrating sustainability considerations into programme monitoring.

Implementation will be carried out in collaboration with academic and research institutions, and development partners, to strengthen technical capacities, enhance methodological rigor and ensure alignment with international accountability standards.</narrative>
  </description>
